Package: SVF
Type: Package
Title: Support Vector Frontier
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Dasha Ivanova, Daniel Valero-Carreras, Juan Aparicio and Nadia M. Guerrero
Maintainer: The package maintainer <yourself@somewhere.net>
Description: Support Vector Frontier (SVF) is a machine learning technique, based on Support Vector Machines (SVM), used for the estimation of production functions. This technique allows the determination of a production function, satisfying the usual axioms of microeconomics (upper enveloping of the data, monotonicity and concavity) through a data-driven approach, like machine learning techniques, generating a step function as a predictor at a first stage. At a second stage, the convexification of the step function generates a piece-wise linear predictor of the production function. These shapes are similar to the estimators derived from FDH and DEA techniques but they do not suffer the problem of overfitting that it affects to these methods.
